<title>FRANCE: SocGen downgrades BNP - fund managers.</title>
<headline>SocGen downgrades BNP - fund managers.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Societe Generale has downgraded its BNP stock rating to &quot;neutral&quot; from &quot;outperform&quot; on the grounds that the bank faces strategic problems in the wake of the Axa /UAP merger pact, fund managers said.</p>
<p>BNP shares were up 1.00 percent at 211.9 francs while the CAC 40 leading share index was up 1.22 percent at 1515 GMT.</p>
<p>The fund managers said Societe Generale brokerage Delahaye was also citing the possibility of the Axa/UAP group divesting its BNP holding.</p>
</text>
